    <!--            LSPOSED MODULE SCOPE            -->
    <!-- ========================================== -->
    <!--
        LSPosed module load scope (xposedscope): any package a user can enable in
        the app must appear here, or LSPosed never loads the module into that
        process. The framework treats these recommended entries as mandatory, so
        every entry here is force-selected in the manager and cannot be unticked.

        com.catsmoker.app is deliberately NOT listed: the manager locks every
        recommended entry as selected, so listing ourselves forced CatSmoker to
        appear selected with no way to deselect it. Detection does not need the
        entry — Vector always loads a module into its own app anyway ("Always in
        scope" on the manager scope screen), which keeps the heartbeat working —
        and the module installs no spoof hooks in its own process in any case
        (NEVER_SPOOF_PACKAGES plus the own-package early return in LSPosedModule).

        This is the only array in the file. Per-game metadata lives in Kotlin —
        EditGameFilesViewModel.initializeGameConfigs and GameType — so there is
        nothing here to keep index-synchronised with anything else.
    -->
